(Bug #91, the map half. LANGUAGE.md, Maps: "A missing key does not crash:
 the lookup yields 0 and sets the error flag, so an `on error` handler can
 react." That 0 is the number 0, and the manual is right about it - a `map`
 read leaves its runtime tag beside the value, so printing a missing key
 still prints 0. What broke was the read landing in a slot whose declared
 type is a pointer: a `text`, `list` or `map` destination stored the 0 and
 dereferenced it on the first read. Each destination now takes its own
 type's empty value, the same one an unwritten slot of that type holds.)

(A map no static proof can close: the literal's value types differ, and
 `Set` can insert any key at all.)
a map called found is {"a": "apple", "counted so far": 2}.
Set found's "b" to "banana".

(The working neighbour: a key the map holds is unchanged.)
a text called present is found's "a".
Print "present: {present}".

(The headline: a key it does not hold, into a text.)
a text called absent is found's "zebra".
Print "absent: [{absent}]".

(Reassignment is the declaration's twin.)
a text called seeded is "seed".
Set seeded to found's "zebra".
Print "reassigned: [{seeded}]".

(Printing the read itself is tag-driven and always was: the manual's 0.)
Print "printed direct: " without newline.
Print found's "zebra".

(A number destination takes that same 0 - the manual's own sentence.)
a number called counted is found's "zebra".
Print "number destination: {counted}".

(A map of lists: the empty list, not a null one.)
a list called apples is ["braeburn"].
a map called baskets is {"a": apples}.
(#72 proves this literal map has no "zebra" and refuses a list
 destination - its own compile_fail case. #91 owns the unprovable half, so a
 Set that never runs reaches the map and the proof is withheld.)
a number called 'never set' is 0.
While 'never set' is less than 0,
    Set baskets's "zebra" to apples,
    Set 'never set' to 'never set' add 1.
a list called 'no basket' is baskets's "zebra".
Print "list destination: {'no basket'}".

(A map of maps: the empty map.)
a map called 'apple facts' is {"colour": "red"}.
a map called facts is {"a": 'apple facts'}.
(The same withholding for `facts`, for the same reason.)
a number called 'never touched' is 0.
While 'never touched' is less than 0,
    Set facts's "zebra" to {"seed": 1},
    Set 'never touched' to 'never touched' add 1.
a map called 'no facts' is facts's "zebra".
Print "map destination: {'no facts'}".

(The empty value is a real collection, so it can be grown afterwards.)
Append "windfall" to 'no basket'.
Print "grown after the miss: {'no basket'}".

(And the miss is still an error.)
a text called 'last miss' is found's "zebra".
On error Print "the error flag was set".
